   "date": "2017-09-09T14:21:28Z",
   "subject": "Re: [brms-users] Prediction of future data",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">You could use the median or mean of the sei in your data set to get the precision of an average study. <br><br>I assume though that you rather want to use &quot;fitted&quot; instead of &quot;predict&quot; in order not to include the sampling error in your predictions. In this case, you still need to include sei in your newdata, but it won&#39;t affect the results.<br></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
