"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pub_year </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2017</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2018</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                      mod_1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><font color=\"#006666\"><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span></font><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><font color=\"#006666\"><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span></font><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                      mod_2 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                      </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>predict</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> newdata </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> newdata</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span></pre></div></code></div> </div><div>but I get this error:</div><div><div>&quot;Error: The following variables are missing in &#39;data&#39;: &#39;sei&#39;&quot;</div></div><div><br></div><div>The the sei is unknown so I&#39;m not sure what to enter - does anyone have any clues at all?</div><div><br></div><div>Many thanks in advance!</div><span><font color=\"#888888\"><div><br></div><div>Oliver</div></font></span></div></blockquote></div></div>"
